# public-repo-guard exclusions (scripts/public-repo-guard/content-policy.sh).
# One glob per line; lines starting with # are comments.

# knowledge/mcp-tools.json is a byte-for-byte copy of the LIVE, PUBLIC response
# from `GET https://api.wave.online/mcp` (anyone can curl this endpoint with no
# auth — see knowledge/mcp-tools.meta.json for the fetch command + sha256). Its
# top-level "name" field is that public API's own self-reported server name,
# which happens to string-match an entry in this org's private-repo blocklist
# even though the value is a live, publicly-served API response field, not a
# reference to an internal repo. It cannot carry an inline `# guard:allow`
# comment (this is JSON), and editing the byte content would invalidate the
# sha256 provenance the wave.ask grounding contract depends on
# (src/knowledge.ts / knowledge/mcp-tools.meta.json) — so the file is excluded
# here instead of altered.
knowledge/mcp-tools.json
